# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=confluence (The Confluence),
# spec=rogue:assassination, style=idle, size=10, difficulty=normal,
# view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# The Confluence has two prior appearances on record and neither is idle:
# 2026-09-26-41.play (mash, mode=raid) wiped at 84.2s with the boss at 23%
# and three of ten dead including the player itself; 2026-09-27-9.play (good,
# mode=walk, reached via an evening) killed it clean with the whole raid
# alive. Both of those left an idle/good/mash triangle with idle missing --
# this is the first true mode=raid idle pull of this specific boss, and it
# matters because docs/upkeep.md's own "raid rewarding play" table has
# Confluence at played=72%/idle=18%, a +54 gap, the opposite direction from
# nearly everything direction.md's line 1 has found. The mash pull already
# showed an active-ish style losing most of the raid here, which is
# suggestive that idle might lose too -- if so this would be only the second
# boss (after Bloodgorged's fester) to meet line 1's own disprove condition.
# src/sim/boss.ts's own comment on this fight (read after the 2026-09-26 mash
# pull) says its demand "is not about where the raid is standing... it asks
# about the geometry between the fight's own bodies" -- an infection mark
# that must not end up near another mark. idle never moves at all, so if
# marks are meant to be walked apart this is the style with no way to answer
# that demand whatsoever.
#
# Reached the documented way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and
# everything below it, since a fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10N.
open #b=confluence&s=10&h=0
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play idle 130
bill
state
shot mid1

play idle 130
bill
state
says
shot end
